## 0. Context you must internalize first

Phase 10 made bot CRUD and historical/paper/walk-forward/Monte-Carlo *backtesting* fully real (Supabase + FastAPI engine). The Live tab (`components/bot/live-tab.tsx`) and the global `/app/live` "Aether View" are still 100% deterministic mock data, seeded from `hashString(bot.id)` (Prompt 03). There is no actual live/paper execution loop anywhere in the system yet.

**Critical design constraint — read before writing any code:** do not build this as raw WebSocket exchange streaming. That is a much larger, riskier lift than this phase should attempt, and it isn't what the existing codebase is set up for. Instead, notice that `apps/engine/requirements.txt` already includes `apscheduler>=3.10.4`, which is not currently used anywhere — this is a strong signal that the intended design for "live" is a **scheduled polling loop**: every N minutes (matching the bot's candle resolution, 15m), fetch the latest closed candle for each live bot's symbol, execute one bar of that bot's compiled graph against its persisted position state, and write the result. The frontend polls a REST endpoint for the latest state — no WebSocket push required from the engine to the browser either.

This mirrors exactly how `apps/engine/app/engine/backtest_runner.py`'s `simulate_historical_pass` already works, just triggered by a scheduler instead of a loop over historical rows, and running forever (until stopped) instead of over a fixed date range.

