## 9. Acceptance checklist

- [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` (web) and a clean Python import check (engine, same pattern as Phase 10's verification) both pass.
- [ ] Running an existing historical backtest produces identical metrics before and after the Task 2 refactor (spot-check one bot/config pair pre- and post-refactor).
- [ ] Starting a live session on a bot with a validation-blocking graph is rejected with a clear error, not silently started.
- [ ] Starting a live session twice on the same bot (e.g., two tabs) results in a clean 409 on the second attempt, not two scheduler jobs or a DB error leaking to the user.
- [ ] After starting, `bots.status` becomes `live` and a `live_sessions` row exists with `status = 'running'`.
- [ ] Waiting past a 15-minute boundary produces a new `live_equity_points` row and, if the graph's risk gate approved a trade, a `live_trades` row — verify directly in Supabase, not just in the UI.
- [ ] The Stop Bot kill switch immediately sets `live_sessions.status = 'stopped'`, `bots.status = 'paused'`, and the scheduler stops ticking that bot (no further rows appear after stopping).
- [ ] Restarting the FastAPI engine process while a bot is live resumes ticking it (scheduler re-registration on startup) without requiring the user to click Stop/Start again.
- [ ] A bot whose live tick throws (e.g., transient Binance fetch failure) flips to `status = 'error'` with a stored `error_message`, and does not continue silently retrying forever.
- [ ] The Live tab and `/app/live` show real, polled data — verify by manually starting a live session and watching a new equity point appear without a page reload.
- [ ] The "Paper trading only" banner is still present, unconditional, on every live-related view.

